<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Aggregated Tables</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We include in this section, under Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ C.2 Aggregated Tables ‣ Appendix C Tables and Graphs ‣ Reasoning with Preference Constraints: A Benchmark for Language Models in Many-to-One Matching Markets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> the aggregated results across the 369 instances, when are of them are valid, for each prompt strategy and model combination.
While our figures included in the paper represent very well the data by number of students and preference types, this table allows to have a more broad view of the overall performances.</p>
</div>
