</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Iterative Prompting Tables</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ RQ3: Can iterative prompting help LLM achieve higher performances through self-verification and correction? ‣ 4 Empirical Evaluation ‣ Reasoning with Preference Constraints: A Benchmark for Language Models in Many-to-One Matching Markets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> showed the main conclusions we can draw from iterative prompting, we present here the exact performances for role-based prompting, but also for every other prompt to show that the conclusions drawn before stay relevant with other prompts.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T5.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
