<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Graphs</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While the Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ RQ2: How does the prompting strategy and model choice affect the quality of the generated matchings? ‣ 4 Empirical Evaluation ‣ Reasoning with Preference Constraints: A Benchmark for Language Models in Many-to-One Matching Markets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> presented the trend for every prompt, the Figure <a href="#A3.F16" title="Figure 16 ‣ C.4 Graphs ‣ Appendix C Tables and Graphs ‣ Reasoning with Preference Constraints: A Benchmark for Language Models in Many-to-One Matching Markets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A3.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ C.4 Graphs ‣ Appendix C Tables and Graphs ‣ Reasoning with Preference Constraints: A Benchmark for Language Models in Many-to-One Matching Markets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> show the detailed results for every prompt, under both complexity dimensions, the number of students and the preference types.</p>
</div>
